# Optional — any of these enables MODE B (live environmental data).
# Tried in order: OpenAQ, then PurpleAir, then WAQI.

# Get a free key at https://explore.openaq.org/register. Aggregates real
# government/reference-grade stations where a provider covers the area;
# Malaysia coverage was not confirmed during development (see
# lib/liveOpenAQ.ts) — falls through cleanly if nothing is nearby.
# OPENAQ_API_KEY=

# Get a free key at https://develop.purpleair.com/. Real sensor coverage
# exists in Klang Valley/Kuala Lumpur. Read lib/livePurpleAir.ts for the
# accuracy caveat (consumer-grade, uncorrected — reads high in humidity).
# PURPLEAIR_API_KEY=

# Get a free token at https://aqicn.org/data-platform/token/. Read
# lib/liveEnvironment.ts for the legal/usage constraints (non-commercial,
# no caching/archiving of the raw feed, attribution required) before using
# this beyond local development or research demonstration.
# WAQI_TOKEN=

# Optional — enables live road-traffic data (TomTom Flow Segment Data),
# replacing the synthetic hour/road-type traffic model that otherwise
# feeds the exposure model and route travel times. Get a free key (no
# credit card required, 2,500 requests/day) at
# https://developer.tomtom.com/. Read lib/liveTraffic.ts for the request-
# budget and terms-of-use notes before using this beyond local development
# or research demonstration.
# TOMTOM_API_KEY=
